ARCHIVE -- SUNAGAKURE CASUALTY SUMMARY, GREAT SHINOBI WARS

Maintained by the memorial office. This summary records the toll borne by the
Hidden Sand across the great wars fought among the shinobi nations. Names are
held in the sealed memorial register; this document reports figures and lessons
only.

Recorded burdens:
- The Puppet Brigade suffered heavily in open-desert engagements, where master
  puppeteers were prime targets for enemy assassination squads.
- Wind-user attrition was high against lightning-nature opponents in prolonged
  campaigns.
- Postwar hardship and reduced Daimyo funding compounded the losses, straining
  the village for a generation.

Lessons carried forward: disperse high-value puppeteers, never commit the
village's jinchuriki lightly, and preserve the alliance that spares Sand blood.
The fallen are honored at the memorial each year. Filed to archive.
